Proposed (11.1s): Use for ANY work in an OCaml project that uses dune (look for `dune-project` file, `.ml`/`.mli` files, or `lib/`+`test/` dirs). This is the default test/build loop for OCaml+dune work — invoke it proactively, don't wait to be asked. Triggers include: running tests or builds, TDD work, fixing bugs, checking that code compiles, verifying renames/refactors, working through OCaml exercises, getting started in a freshly cloned dune project, or explicitly setting up/starting a "dune watcher". Covers launching `dune runtest -w`, the wait-for-rebuild protocol after edits, and what one-shot commands to avoid while it's running. Do NOT use for: OCaml questions unrelated to a dune project (syntax, translation, language help), reading/explaining `dune-project` or `.opam` file contents, non-OCaml build tooling (vite, flask, webpack), or anything where no dune project is present.

